      "writtenOn": "2023-01-26T20:40:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can `isSynthesizedOutParamArg` possibly be true for a global? It seems impossible to me. I think you could probably restructure this so that `fOutParamArgVars.contains` is only checked in the else-case for `Variable::Storage::kLocal`-typed variables (and in the other cases, I suppose we could assert `!fOutParamArgVars.contains` if want to be sure).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 999,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 999,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "71abaf4a5669c8b6e7c05b0de7535df075bda52b",
